-- title:
--   The slot-split quadratic is nonpositive on its balanced hyperplane
-- statement:
--   Let $n,r\in\mathbb N$, $E=\{0,\ldots,n-1\}$, and $\widehat E=E\times\{0,1\}$. Let $o_1,o_2$ be Boolean subset oracles and $q\in\mathbb Q$. For $S\subseteq\widehat E$, let $\mathsf r(S)$ be the program’s paired-rank value and put $v(S)=q^{\max(n-\mathsf r(S),0)}$. For label sets $B,R\subseteq\widehat E$, a set $U\subseteq E$, and label $h$, define the completion family $$\mathcal C(B,R,U;h)=\{B\cup(R\setminus\{h\})\cup\{(t,b_t):t\in U\}:b:E\to\{0,1\}\}.$$ Its slot total is the real number $$s(B,R,U;h)=\sum_{S\in\mathcal C(B,R,U;h)}v(S),$$ counting each resulting state once. Assume $M_1,M_2$ are matroids with full ground set $E$, common rank $r$, and exact independence oracles $o_1,o_2$, and assume $0<q\le1$. Assume $B\cap R=\varnothing$, neither label of any $t\in U$ belongs to $B\cup R$, and $$|B|+|R|+|U|=n+1.$$ Choose $t\in U$ and put $$s_a(h)=s(B,R\cup\{(t,0)\},U\setminus\{t\};h),\quad s_b(h)=s(B,R\cup\{(t,1)\},U\setminus\{t\};h),$$ $$u=s(B,R\cup\{(t,0)\},U\setminus\{t\};(t,0)).$$ Define $V_{hh}=0$; for $h\ne l$, let $V_{hl}$ sum $v(S)$ over the distinct states $$S=B\cup(R\setminus\{h,l\})\cup\{(t,0),(t,1)\}\cup\{(s,b_s):s\in U\setminus\{t\}\}.$$ For any real label potential $H$ and real $x,y$ satisfying $$\sum_{h\in R}(s_a(h)+s_b(h))H_h+u(x+y)=0,$$ one has $$\sum_{h,l\in R}V_{hl}H_hH_l+2x\sum_{h\in R}s_b(h)H_h+2y\sum_{h\in R}s_a(h)H_h+2uxy\le0.$$ This is the quadratic input to the recursive split estimate.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/meelgroup/counting-matroid/blob/dd16a4628fdb095c58fe0f3dfd8e353c6e97443c/CountingMatroid/Analysis/DefectSlotSplitSignature.lean#L131-L292

